### The session cookie is marked Secure, so it is only ever set over HTTPS.
### Pointing this at the http:// port makes sign-in appear to succeed while the
### browser silently discards the cookie and every later request arrives anonymous.
@ExamArchive_HostAddress = https://localhost:7294

### ==================== Sign in ====================
### Only staff have accounts. Students never sign in — uploading is anonymous and
### browsing is public. Both accounts exist only in Development and are created by
### SeedData; the password is printed as a warning at startup.
### Everything under "Moderation" below returns 401 until one of these has run.

### Sign in as a moderator — unlocks the moderation section
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "moderator",
  "password": "Lozinka!12345"
}

### Sign in as an admin — same powers today, plus the configuration work to come
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "Lozinka!12345"
}

### Wrong password — same message as an unknown username, on purpose
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "moderator",
  "password": "wrong"
}

### Who am I? 401 when not signed in — the cookie is HttpOnly, so this is the
### only way a frontend can find out.
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me
Accept: application/json

### Change your own password. Requires the current one — a session cookie proves
### the browser signed in once, not that the person at the keyboard owns the
### account. Minimum 12 characters for the new one.
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/auth/change-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "Lozinka!12345",
  "newPassword": "NovaLozinka2026"
}

### Same password back again — refused, so a change that did nothing is not
### mistaken for one that worked
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/auth/change-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "NovaLozinka2026",
  "newPassword": "NovaLozinka2026"
}

### Sign out
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout

### ==================== Browsing (anonymous) ====================

### Majors in Bachelor's
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/majors?studiesId=1
Accept: application/json

### Majors in Master's
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/majors?studiesId=2
Accept: application/json

### Every major
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/majors
Accept: application/json

### Subjects in Computer Science (id 1) — note YearOfStudy
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/subjects?majorId=1
Accept: application/json

### Subjects in Software Engineering (id 2) — Databases lands a year later here
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/subjects?majorId=2
Accept: application/json

### Approved papers for Databases (id 5) — the Pending 2025 resit is filtered out
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/papers?subjectId=5
Accept: application/json

### Approved papers for Data Structures (id 4) — the Rejected 2024 final is filtered out
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/papers?subjectId=4
Accept: application/json

### Linear Algebra (id 2) — taught in two majors, but the archive is empty
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/papers?subjectId=2
Accept: application/json

### Pages of an approved paper
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/papers/1/files
Accept: application/json

### One page, opened in the browser
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/papers/1/files/1

### The same page, forced to download
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/papers/1/files/1?download=true

### Check on an anonymous submission using the claim code from the upload response.
### Replace the code below with the "claimToken" the upload actually returned —
### these are random, so this exact one will 404.
### Case, dashes and O-for-0 are all forgiven, so it can be typed as written down.
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/papers/status/DHA22-9Z2JC-0KDFM-73RZ3
Accept: application/json

### An unknown code — same 404 as a malformed one, on purpose
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/papers/status/AAAAA-BBBBB-CCCCC-DDDDD
Accept: application/json

### ==================== Account management (Admin only) ====================
### Sign in as admin first. A moderator gets 403 on everything here.

### Every staff account, including deactivated ones
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/users
Accept: application/json

### Create an account for a professor. The response carries a generated password —
### it is shown once and never again, so read it out before closing the window.
### The account can sign in but do nothing else until it replaces that password.
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "prof.jovanovic",
  "role": 3
}

### Promote to admin. This is how the archive stops depending on one administrator.
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/users/3/role
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": 2
}

### Somebody forgot their password. This is the whole of password recovery.
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/users/3/reset-password

### Somebody left. Deactivate rather than delete, so their past decisions keep
### their name on them. Refused with 409 if this is the last active admin.
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/users/3/deactivate

### Somebody came back. The password is untouched.
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/users/3/activate

### ==================== Moderation (Moderator or Admin) ====================
### 401 with no session. 403 would mean a signed-in account without the role,
### which cannot happen while Moderator and Admin are the only two.

### The review queue, longest-waiting first
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/moderation/papers
Accept: application/json

### Papers already rejected
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/moderation/papers?status=Rejected
Accept: application/json

### Pages of a submitted paper — answers for pending papers, unlike the browse API
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/moderation/papers/28/files
Accept: application/json

### Preview a submission in the browser, no download step
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/moderation/papers/28/files/1

### Approve a paper — it becomes visible through the browse API
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/moderation/papers/28/approve

### Reject a paper. The reason is required and shown to the submitter.
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/moderation/papers/29/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Page 2 is upside down and unreadable. Please re-photograph it."
}

### Rejected papers, with the reason each was turned down for
GET {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/moderation/papers?status=Rejected
Accept: application/json

### Staff upload — published immediately, skips the queue.
### The most dangerous endpoint here: it writes to the public archive with no
### review. Sign in as moderator or admin above first, or this returns 401.
POST {{ExamArchive_HostAddress}}/api/moderation/papers/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="SubjectId"

5
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="ExamType"

Final
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="Month"

6
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="Year"

2026
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="Files"; filename="page1.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./uploads/2026/databases-final-2026-01-12b6010d.pdf
------Boundary--

###
